    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="0357" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v02p1/pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">S/S–NSC files, lot 66 D 148, “Solarium”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum for the Record by the Special Assistant to
                        the President for National Security Affairs (Cutler)</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d65-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Personal and
                            Confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-05-15">15 May 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list rendition="#flush" subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <item>Subject:</item>
                    <item>Solarium Project</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>This memorandum is an initial report by the Working Committee of the
                        National Security Council appointed to arrange the detailed plans for
                        carrying out the above project (The Acting Secretary of State, General W. B. Smith; the Director for
                        Central Intelligence, Allen W.
                            Dulles; and the Special Assistant to the President for
                        National Security Affairs, Robert
                            Cutler.)</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>In accordance with the President’s instructions, as reported to the
                        Council on 15 May 1953,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d65-f2"/> the following have
                        been requested to act as the Panel to draft precise and detailed terms of
                        reference for each alternative (see par 2a, Solarium Project Memo of 9 May
                            1953<anchor n="3" xml:id="d65-f3"/>), and have accepted the assignment: <list>
                            <item>General James H. Doolittle, <hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Chairman</hi></item>
                            <item>Robert Amory,
                                Jr.</item>
                            <item>Lt. General L. L.
                                    Lemnitzer</item>
                            <item>Dean Rusk</item>
                            <item>Admiral Leslie C. Stevens</item>
                        </list></item>
                    <pb facs="0358" n="328" xml:id="pg328"/>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The Panel will convene in Room 376, Executive Offices Building,
                        Washington, D.C. on Monday, 25 May 1953, at 9:30 A.M. o’clock. The members
                        of the Working Committee will discuss the problem with the Panel at 10:30
                        A.M. o’clock.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>It is anticipated that the Panel will carry on their work continuously
                        until completion, which it is anticipated should be not later than 1 June
                        1953. Office space, secretarial assistance, required source materials, etc.,
                        will be provided in the National Security Council Area. Mr. T. M.
                            Koons, NSC Special Staff
                        Member (Executive 3–7491, Extension 3675), will act as Executive Secretary
                        for Solarium Project.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>No publicity of any kind should be given to, or mention made of, the
                        project. It is essential to success that the most complete discretion be
                        observed. For that reason, no further communication will be sent from this
                        office. If communication regarding the above arrangements is necessary,
                        please telephone to the undersigned or Mr. Koons
                        (referring only to Solarium).</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert
                                Cutler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
